Unix utility 'vt'

The Unix utility 'vt' switches the physical display to one of the eight virtual terminals
Hexagon provides, numbered 0 to 7. Each virtual terminal keeps its own content, cursor and
colors, so the processes running on one go on running while another is shown.

A virtual terminal never switched to before starts blank. Switching back to one already in
use restores whatever was left on it. The same switch can be made at any moment from the
keyboard, with Ctrl and the function key matching the index, so Ctrl+F1 reaches terminal 0.

The process that calls this utility is not moved to the terminal being shown. It keeps
writing to the terminal it was already attached to, which 'vt' does not change.

USAGE:

vt <index>

Example of use:

vt 2

It brings virtual terminal 2 to the display.

For more information, enter 'vt ?' or 'vt --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix Mineru development branch (2026).

